{"brief": "ROBOT NAVIGATION BRIEF

Develop navigation logic for a mobile robot.

The robot receives information about whether the path
in front, to the left, and to the right is blocked.

It may also receive information about whether its goal
is ahead, to the left, or to the right.

The robot should prefer moving toward its goal whenever
this can be done safely.

It must never move into a blocked direction.

If there is no safe direction available, it must stop.

The navigation component will eventually be tested in
multiple simulated environments.", "requirements": {"goal": "Navigate towards the goal position if safe and possible", "allowed_actions": ["FORWARD", "LEFT", "RIGHT", "STOP"], "safe_stop": true, "avoid_obstacles": true}, "plan": {"strategy": "Prefer a clear goal direction first, otherwise use the first unblocked fallback direction, and STOP if no direction is clear.", "decisions": [{"when": "CLEAR_TARGET", "select": "TARGET"}, {"when": "NO_CLEAR_TARGET", "select": "FIRST_CLEAR"}], "fallback_order": ["FORWARD", "LEFT", "RIGHT"], "stop_condition": "NO_CLEAR_EXIT"}, "code": "def navigate(obstacles, target=None):
    if target is not None and not obstacles[target]:
        return target
    for direction in ["FORWARD", "LEFT", "RIGHT"]:
        if not obstacles[direction]:
            return direction
    return "STOP"

def decide_next_move(state):
    blocked_paths = {"FORWARD": state["front_blocked"], "LEFT": state["left_blocked"], "RIGHT": state["right_blocked"]}
    if state["goal_ahead"] and not blocked_paths["FORWARD"]:
        return navigate(blocked_paths, "FORWARD")
    if state["goal_on_left"] and not blocked_paths["LEFT"]:
        return navigate(blocked_paths, "LEFT")
    if state["goal_on_right"] and not blocked_paths["RIGHT"]:
        return navigate(blocked_paths, "RIGHT")
    return navigate(blocked_paths)
"}
